in the year 1949 bill bladdy was an  undergraduate at Georgetown University  the oldest Jesuit school in the country  while in his religious class his  religious instructor told him a story  about a demonic possession and exorcism  of a fourteen-year-old boy now this  story was widely publicized on the front  page of the Washington Post and a number  of other newspapers and the story flatly  stated that there was a  fourteen-year-old boy in Silver Springs  Silver Spring Maryland who was possessed  by the devil and exorcised by a group of  priests in an Alexian Brothers Hospital  in st. Louis Missouri  bloody and I guess everyone in his class  felt that if this story was true if this  could possibly be true it would be  religious nirvana  and so he set out to try and get as much  information about it as he could and of  course the church would say nothing the  church would not and rightly so you know  to maintain the privacy of the family  they gave out in fact whenever they were  asked a lot of false incorrect  information they said that this happened  in Silver Spring Maryland it actually  happened in a smaller town nearby called  Cottage City Maryland but the church did  everything it could to protect the  family and the boy the boy was evidently  successfully exorcised and he then later  in life went to work for NASA and he  worked for NASA for 25 years and retired  owning a lot of  patents for his inventions the family  was Lutheran they weren't Catholic they  went to their Lutheran minister who said  we don't have anything to deal with this  young man's affliction so try the  Catholic Church which they did at the  Washington DC diocese now as I say  bloody couldn't get any of the facts so  he decided to write his novel as fiction  The Exorcist is a work of fiction  whether you believe in possession and  exorcism is totally up to you it has to  do with the mystery of faith  but none of us have any of these answers  none of us nobody no one who's ever  lived none of the greatest philosophers  who ever lived  know if there's a heaven or a hell or  God or angels and demons it is a matter  of your belief system or no belief  system but I think one of the reasons  you're here tonight is because we're all  curious about the possibility of the  supernatural I certainly was
 

